Homepage: https://github.com/farhadzaidi/snappy
Description: Snappy arranges windows into zones
 Pick a layout for each display, then drag a window with a key held, or press
 a shortcut, and it snaps into place. Snappy also swaps windows, moves focus
 between them, and keeps workspaces of windows to switch between. It never
 uses the network, and never reads window titles, window contents, or what
 you type.
 .
 Works on GNOME and KDE Plasma on Wayland, and on X11. The commands are
 snappy, which runs in the background, and snappy-app, its window.
